I get off at the Fort Kochi boat jetty.
A small Sunday market is happening nearby.
Due to the rain, there is a lot of water on the road.
Even so, there are many people there.
I walk past each of the stalls.
There are a lot of fruits here.
Over there, many types of baskets can be seen.
I pick up a small basket in my hand.
"Brother, what is the price of this basket?" I ask the seller.
"For that, one hundred rupees," he replies.
A big basket is hanging behind him.
"And for that big basket?" I ask, pointing to it.
"That is two hundred rupees," he says.
Then I stand in front of another stall.
There is good cardamom tea powder there.
A few weeks ago, my mother had asked about this.
I buy a packet of tea powder for my mother.
